From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] With $PRO1X_OSK_MANUAL, text fields neither show nor hide it

The surface follows the input method's active state: every change of focus
showed or hid the keyboard, and resized the windows with it.  In Sway it is
now only shown and hidden by hand, through SetVisible (author, 2026-11-03).
Phosh and the greeter run it without the variable, and keep the default.
---
--- a/src/phosh-osk-stevia.c
+++ b/src/phosh-osk-stevia.c
@@ -203,6 +203,11 @@
     return TRUE;
   }
 
+  if (g_getenv ("PRO1X_OSK_MANUAL")) {
+    g_value_set_boolean (to_value, pos_input_surface_get_visible (self->input_surface));
+    return TRUE;
+  }
+
   enabled = pos_input_surface_get_screen_keyboard_enabled (self->input_surface);
 
   if (self->activation_filter && !pos_activation_filter_allow_active (self->activation_filter))
